## 4. MODULE-BY-MODULE TECHNICAL BREAKDOWN

### 4.1. Core Portal & Department Switcher
- **Primary Files**: `index.php`, `fab-nav.php`, `footer.php`, `theme-toggle.php`, `assets/css/portal.css`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Acts as the central navigation springboard for the entire university department portal.
  - Features an interactive 3D mouse-tilt terminal interface showing departmental programs (B.Tech, Diploma, ICT), vision, mission, and HOD leadership details.
  - Provides a toggle between **Information Technology** (Red Theme Accent) and **Computer Engineering** (Blue Theme Accent).
  - Floating Action Button (`fab-nav.php`) gives one-click sticky access to all sub-modules from any page.
  - Unified theme switcher (`theme-toggle.php`) enables switching between dark glassmorphism and light mode with instant CSS custom property reconfiguration.

### 4.2. Daily Faculty Workload & CTL Report
- **Primary Files**: `report.php`, `assets/css/style.css`, `assets/js/otp-verify.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Detailed web form enabling faculty members to log daily lectures, labs, seminar sessions, and academic achievements.
  - Captures: Academic Year, Date, Faculty Name/Email, Report Type, Title, Time Duration, Venue, Program, Semester, Division, Batch, Attendance Count, Topics Covered, and Google Drive attachments.
  - **Auto-Save & Draft Recovery**: Real-time `localStorage` autosave prevents data loss in the event of accidental browser close, power failure, or network disruption.
  - **Submission Verification**: If `otp_enabled = 1` in `config.php`, the form triggers a modal 6-digit OTP challenge to the faculty's verified `@gmiu.edu.in` email before allowing final submission.
  - **Simultaneous Dual Delivery**: Upon verification, the form dispatches an HTML summary email to the department admin and streams the record to Google Sheets via `proxy-sheets.php?target=report`.

### 4.3. 6-Digit Email OTP Verification Engine
- **Primary Files**: `otp-service.php`, `assets/js/otp-verify.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - High-security cryptographic one-time password system protecting report submissions from impersonation.
  - Validates recipient domain (`@gmiu.edu.in` required).
  - Enforces a 15-second resend cooldown to prevent email bombing.
  - Generates a 6-digit integer via `random_int(100000, 999999)`.
  - Stores OTP code, generation timestamp, and expiration (`time() + 300`, 5-minute validity) inside `$_SESSION['otp_store'][$email]`.
  - Dispatches custom-styled HTML email via Gmail SMTP using department-specific sender credentials.
  - Returns JSON status codes for clean client-side feedback in the responsive digit-by-digit OTP modal.

### 4.4. Zero-Student Attendance Incident Reporting
- **Primary Files**: `zero-student-report.php`, `assets/js/zero-student-report.js`, `assets/css/zero-student-report.css`, `assets/js/google-apps-script-zero.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Specialized, high-priority reporting tool for classes where zero students attend as per the official timetable.
  - Captures: Incident Date, Start/End Time, Room No., Branch/Program, Semester, Division, Subject, Faculty Name, and Reason/Remarks.
  - **120-Second Anti-Duplicate Filter**: Integrates server-side deduplication via session hash and `uploads/.zs_dedup_cache.json`. Submitting identical reports within 2 minutes is blocked to prevent accidental double-clicks or browser reload duplication.
  - Dispatches an emergency incident alert email to department heads and logs the record to the `Zero Student Log` Google Sheet.

### 4.5. Transactional SMTP Email Service
- **Primary Files**: `send-email.php`, `assets/js/google-apps-script-email-tracker.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Native PHP replacement for legacy Node.js mailers, running asynchronously with `ignore_user_abort(true)` and `set_time_limit(0)`.
  - **Domain Whitelist / Open-Relay Guard**: Strictly verifies that all `to` and `cc` recipients end with `@gmiu.edu.in`. Requests containing external domains are immediately rejected with HTTP 403 Forbidden.
  - **Department Routing**: Dynamically chooses credentials from `config.php`:
    - IT Department: Uses `smtp_email` (`adminit@gmiu.edu.in`) and `smtp_password`.
    - CE Department: Uses `smtp_email_ce` (`admincecse@gmiu.edu.in`) and `smtp_password_ce`.
  - Generates email layouts with responsive HTML tables, badges, timestamp headers, and university branding.
  - Asynchronously pings `mail_tracking_webapp_url` to keep an immutable Google Sheet audit log of all emails sent.

### 4.6. Timetable System & Background Live Sync
- **Primary Files**:
  - `timetable.php` (Faculty timetable viewer)
  - `student-timetable.php` (Student timetable viewer)
  - `sync-timetables.php` (Core Google Sheets synchronizer)
  - `timetable-compiler.php` (Faculty OpenXML to JS compiler)
  - `student-timetable-parser.php` (Student OpenXML to JSON parser)
  - `update-timetable.php` (Webhook / manual sync runner)
  - `assets/js/timetableSync.js` (Client-side auto-sync poller)
  - `assets/js/timetableData.js` (Compiled faculty database)
- **Functionality**:
  - **Faculty Viewer**: Interactive schedule matrix allowing filtering by faculty name, day of week, room number, or subject. Includes weekly workload totals and empty-slot indicators.
  - **Student Viewer**: Filterable timetable by Semester (Sem 1 to Sem 8), Division (Class A, B, C), and Practical Batch.
  - **Cloud Synchronization (`sync-timetables.php`)**:
    - Connects to Google Apps Script endpoints to fetch the latest Excel binaries via Base64 or direct stream.
    - Validates file integrity (`PK\x03\x04` zip header).
    - Compares MD5 checksums to skip redundant compilation if the spreadsheet hasn't changed.
    - Compiles `uploads/timetable/timetable.xlsx` into `assets/js/timetableData.js`.
    - Compiles `uploads/student_timetable/student_timetable.xlsx` into `student_timetable_cache.json`.
  - **Background Polling (`timetableSync.js`)**:
    - Automatically checks for timetable changes every `auto_sync_interval` seconds (default: 300s).
    - Prompts an authentication password modal when an admin initiates a manual cloud sync.

### 4.7. CTL Activity & Google Drive Scanner
- **Primary Files**: `ctlactivity.php`, `ctldrive.php`, `assets/css/ctlactivity.css`, `assets/css/ctldrive.css`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Protected behind `auth-check.php` password barrier.
  - **CTL Activity Dashboard (`ctlactivity.php`)**: Continuous Teaching & Learning monitor tracking syllabus progression, unit plans, and student performance. Supports client-side Excel upload and real-time parsing with SheetJS (`xlsx.full.min.js`).
  - **Drive Folder Scanner (`ctldrive.php`)**: Administrative tool mapping Google Drive shared drives, subject resource folders, lab manuals, and faculty course files.

### 4.8. Faculty Directory & Workload Summary Analytics
- **Primary Files**: `faculty.php`, `workload-summary.php`, `assets/js/facultyData.js`, `assets/css/faculty.css`.
- **Functionality**:
  - **Faculty Directory (`faculty.php`)**: Interactive roster of all department professors, assistant professors, and technical staff, displaying cabin numbers, phone extensions, official emails, designations, and personal Google Drive resource folders.
  - **Workload Summary (`workload-summary.php`)**: Computes total lecture hours, lab hours, and weekly commitment per faculty member from the compiled timetable. Features a clean, ink-friendly black-and-white print stylesheet (`@media print`) for official university submissions.

### 4.9. Academic Calendar & Syllabus/Exam Paper Hub
- **Primary Files**: `calendar.php`, `syllabus-papers.php`, `scrape.php`, `assets/js/calendarData.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - **Academic Calendar (`calendar.php`)**: Monthly visual schedule displaying university holidays, reserved holidays, term start/end dates, mid-semester exam dates, and cultural festivals.
  - **Syllabus & Exam Papers (`syllabus-papers.php`)**: Searchable index of official GMIU course codes, credit distribution tables, and past exam question papers.
  - **CORS Scraper Proxy (`scrape.php`)**: A secure server-side cURL crawler that queries official university examination portals, bypasses CORS restrictions, parses HTML responses, and returns structured JSON to the frontend.

### 4.10. Security, Authentication & Configuration
- **Primary Files**: `config.php`, `auth-check.php`, `auth-login-page.php`, `verify-password.php`.
- **Functionality**:
  - **Master Configuration (`config.php`)**: Houses all sensitive parameters, SMTP app passwords, Google Apps Script URLs, and feature toggles.
  - **Authentication Guard (`auth-check.php`)**: Inspects `$_SESSION['authenticated']`. If locked or expired, renders `auth-login-page.php` with HTTP security headers (`X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`).
  - **Verification API (`verify-password.php`)**: Accepts POST JSON requests with submitted passwords. Validates using `password_verify($password, $hash)` (Bcrypt) and sets session tokens upon success.

### 4.11. Google Apps Script Proxy & Integration Layer
- **Primary Files**: `proxy-sheets.php`, `assets/js/google-apps-script*.js`.
- **Functionality**:
  - Bridges browser AJAX calls with Google Apps Script Web Apps.
  - Shields confidential Google Apps Script deployment URLs from being exposed in browser source code.
  - Implements server-side cURL with follow-redirects (`CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION`) to seamlessly handle Google's 302 redirects to `script.googleusercontent.com`.

